Description: Detects stationary events (stops) and recurrent stop locations in
    GPS or cartesian trajectories. The algorithm operates in two stages. First,
    it identifies stationary events by clustering temporally adjacent points
    that remain within a specified spatial radius for a minimum duration.
    Second, it groups these event centroids into reusable location identifiers
    using two-level Infomap community detection on a radius-neighbour graph.
    The implementation provides an Rcpp-based port of the 'Infostop'
    algorithm described in Aslak et al. (2020) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2003.14370>.
